From: Pharma360 QA Team
Subject: [PATCH 004/05] Fix frontend healthcheck to use curl instead of wget
Date: 2026-11-01

This patch fixes the frontend container healthcheck. The nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged
image doesn't have wget installed and doesn't allow apk add (non-root user).
We use curl which is already available in the image.

---
 docker-compose.yml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/docker-compose.yml b/docker-compose.yml
index abc1234..def5678 100644
--- a/docker-compose.yml
+++ b/docker-compose.yml
@@ -99,7 +99,7 @@ services:
     networks:
       - pharma360-network
     healthcheck:
-      test: ["CMD", "wget", "-q", "--spider", "http://localhost:8080/ || exit 1"]
+      test: ["CMD-SHELL", "curl -f http://localhost:8080/ || exit 1"]
       interval: 30s
       timeout: 10s
       retries: 5
---
To apply this patch:
  cd /workspace/github__DuDuEZN__Pharma-360
  patch -p1 < patches/004-fix-frontend-healthcheck-wget.patch

OR manually apply:
  1. Edit docker-compose.yml
  2. Change line 102 from:
     test: ["CMD", "wget", "-q", "--spider", "http://localhost:8080/ || exit 1"]
     to:
     test: ["CMD-SHELL", "curl -f http://localhost:8080/ || exit 1"]

Note: This change is already applied in the current repository state.
